sentences.text:
Upon hearing the arguments, the Tribunal answered issues as under:
Issue No.1: partly in the affirmative;
Issue No.2: partly in the affirmative;
Issue No.3: as per final order.

MFA No.102193 of 2022 preferred by the Insurance Company is partly allowed;
ii. MFA No.102453 of 2022 preferred by the claimants is dismissed;
iii. Judgment and award dated 02nd February, 2022 passed in MVC No.373 of 2020 is modified by modifying the same by awarding compensation of Rs.28,31,600/- as against Rs.31,34,000/- awarded by the Tribunal;

The compensation amount carries interest at the rate of 6% per annum from the date of petition till its realisation;
v. Respondent Insurance Company is directed to deposit the amount within 60 days from the date of receipt of certified copy of this judgment;
vi. Amount if any in deposit, be transmitted to the Tribunal forthwith for onward disbursal to the claimants;
vii. Apportionment and disbursement of the compensation amount shall be as per the award of the Tribunal;
viii. Registry to draw award accordingly;
ix.

